 {"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1","node":"reviewer","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-09T12:24:25Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"Evidence capture classifies .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md and revisor/prompts/analyze.md as 'loop churn — counts only', but the seed spec (fabro-91ff) explicitly requires changes to those exact files as acceptance criteria (b) and (c). The reviewer then has no diff for a third of the review scope and must re-read the files blind (run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1). Suggestion: the evidence classifier should promote loop files to seed-work review scope when the in-progress seed spec names them as deliverables (path match against the spec text would suffice)."}],"observations":["Verified all three acceptance criteria by direct file reads since prompt diffs were counts-only in the capture; engine-side fix (run_summary_store.rs) verified from the complete diff — SQL broadening matches the waiting-on-child/parked-parent/soft-stop windows named in the spec.","Revisor Step 3.5 adds a read-only `git fetch origin <base-branch>` using the pre-existing engine git credential bridge — a new code path for an existing capability, but read-only and directly mandated by the seed spec (duplicate-run detection requires base-branch state), so treated as spec-recorded rather than an undocumented ADR-0019 capability expansion.","Requirement (b) chose the prompt-guard direction over exposing current_seed_id in the projection, per the seed's 'keep this seed's diff scoped' clause; fabro-9372 still open for the projection key — no drift concern."]}}
