 {"id":"fabro-2eb6","title":"Implementer prompt: rg replace-flag discipline line; retract the false 'sandbox rg unreliable' journal lore","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T11:24:53.610Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T11:32:56.909Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md` add one line: `rg -r <text>` REPLACES matches — never write `rg -rn`; `-n` alone is the line-number flag. In run 01M22X87J1RKQ6A8FZB7RC2RN8 (events seq 140, 158) the implementer ran `rg -rn \"is_engine_stamped_key\"` and `rg -rn \"pub fn is_success\"`; rg parsed `-r n` as replace-with-literal-n, producing `pub fn n(key: &str...)`, which the implementer then misdiagnosed in `.fabro/journal/01M22X87J1RKQ6A8FZB7RC2RN8.jsonl` as 'rg in this sandbox mangled output — cannot be trusted verbatim' (durable false platform lore; cost 2 extra diagnostic rounds). Expected effect: eliminates this error class and stops the false claim from seeding future revision work. Basis: run 01M22X87J1RKQ6A8FZB7RC2RN8, workflow version 14ab451ff2f9375f4927ce7d994c63bc96f48f3c617f3baff15119472f3af3e4, commit 757bd457f0405a9889aa62144ea0c3f60581e655","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-9372","title":"Expose current_seed_id in the fabro_runs_list projection — stop the planner reverse-engineering the seed id","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T11:25:02.438Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T11:52:51.277Z","description":"Engine-side, extend the `fabro_runs_list` run projection to include the run's `current_seed_id`; interim one-liner in `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md` step 4: read it from `.fabro/journal/<run_id>.jsonl` directly. In run 01M22X87J1RKQ6A8FZB7RC2RN8 (events seq 44–59) the planner saw open PR #78, could not map it to a seed (every develop run shares one generic goal), and burned 4 tool calls — journal-dir ls|grep, a junk-matching `fabro-[a-z0-9]{4}` regex, a head of another run's journal — before concluding fabro-fc1b, ~3 extra LLM rounds in its 80 s inference. Expected effect: −3 tool calls and −2 LLM rounds per planner pass whenever any PR is open; removes a fragile heuristic that could mis-skip a valid candidate or miss a real double-pick. Guard lineage (fabro-c419, fabro-06e0, fabro-d0c7) is closed and never covered seed-id mapping. Basis: run 01M22X87J1RKQ6A8FZB7RC2RN8, workflow version 14ab451ff2f9375f4927ce7d994c63bc96f48f3c617f3baff15119472f3af3e4, commit 757bd457f0405a9889aa62144ea0c3f60581e655 FRESH EVIDENCE 2026-09-09 (review 01M22YZBNJ0): the double-pick guard still parses goal prose/journals to map PR->seed; consider also stamping current_seed_id as a run label so the mapping is structural - same goal as the projection field, pick one mechanism in implementation.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-7613","title":"Engine: auto-stamp a painpoint when a stage pages through a preamble blob ref its journal never reported as friction","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T11:25:10.901Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T11:32:57.078Z","description":"In the engine (fabro-workflow), when a stage's tool log shows a read of a `/tmp/fabro/runtime/blobs/...` path, deterministically append a painpoint stub to that stage's journal, or lint the blob-read-with-empty-painpoints mismatch at stage completion (reusing the ContextKeyOmitted lint machinery this very run shipped). In run 01M22X87J1RKQ6A8FZB7RC2RN8 reviewer@1 paged through the demoted 11.6 KB evidence capture (seq 291) — under its own 16 KB inline ceiling yet blob-ref'd by the aggregate 24 KB budget — while its journal reported `painpoints: []` (seq 309) despite reviewer.md's workaround-is-a-painpoint rule; the improve loop's friction channel silently dropped a real recurring event. Orthogonal to open fabro-50de (prompt-side classification) and closed fabro-176b (relaying declared painpoints): this detects the workaround engine-side. Expected effect: evidence-pipe friction reaches the improve loop deterministically instead of via self-report that demonstrably failed here. Basis: run 01M22X87J1RKQ6A8FZB7RC2RN8, workflow version 14ab451ff2f9375f4927ce7d994c63bc96f48f3c617f3baff15119472f3af3e4, commit 757bd457f0405a9889aa62144ea0c3f60581e655","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-91ff","title":"engine: conductor passes overlapped despite on_overlap=skip — double develop claim on fabro-8bf4 (PR #84 vs #86)","status":"in_progress","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T11:25:52.520Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T12:02:05.569Z","description":"Incident 2026-09-09 11:00-11:20Z (caught by line-watch): two conductor passes ran in PARALLEL although the conductor automation has on_overlap=skip — pass X 01M22X67GYXC (started ~10:53Z, still running at 11:20Z) and pass Y 01M22VF9PWJH (11:14-11:39Z). Their develop legs both claimed fabro-8bf4: X's child 01M22X87J1R planner at 11:02:37Z journaled the in-flight guard saw only PR #78 ('no skip needed'); its PR #86 opened 11:16:45Z (run end). Y's child 01M22VHABGCN claimed the same seed ~11:15Z - in the mid-flight window where the seed has NO open PR yet - and PR #84 merged first (396f5ca3e). Result: two green but overlapping implementations of one lint (envelope.rs/context.rs); PR #86 closed as duplicate. Cost: one wasted develop run (~15 min + LLM spend) + duplicate PR handling.\n\nTwo coupled gaps:\n(a) OVERLAP SEMANTICS: investigate why on_overlap=skip admitted pass Y while pass X was active. Hypotheses: overlap check considers only actively-executing (not waiting/parked-on-child) runs; or the run_wait blocked-instantly misjudgment (open fabro-ee5d) made X look terminal to the scheduler. Reproduce from run states + automation trigger log.\n(b) MID-FLIGHT BLIND SPOT: the planner in-flight guard (fabro_runs_list -> open run-linked PRs, fabro-06e0/c419) cannot see a seed claimed by a RUNNING develop run whose PR does not exist yet (~15 min window per pass). Fix direction: the guard must also exclude seeds claimed by running develop runs - fabro_runs_list already returns run status/workflow/parent - or the conductor must serialize develop legs engine-side so parallel claims are impossible.\n\nExpected effect: the double-implement class (fabro-22e4 lineage) stays closed even under overlapping passes; no wasted runs/PRs. Evidence: journals of 01M22X87J1R (planner observation) and 01M22VHABGCN, PRs #84/#86, fabro ps -a timeline. THIRD SURFACE (line-watch 2026-09-09): the revisor reviewing the duplicate run at 11:21Z also missed it - its review (PR #87) never mentions #84/#86 because the run's basis predates #84's merge. Add to the revisor/analyst checklist: before distilling a develop run, check whether the run's seed is already closed on the base branch (duplicate-run detection), so a duplicate run cannot pass review as healthy.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"assignee":"fabro"}
