asses; no wasted runs/PRs. Evidence: journals of 01M22X87J1R (planner observation) and 01M22VHABGCN, PRs #84/#86, fabro ps -a timeline. THIRD SURFACE (line-watch 2026-09-09): the revisor reviewing the duplicate run at 11:21Z also missed it - its review (PR #87) never mentions #84/#86 because the run's basis predates #84's merge. Add to the revisor/analyst checklist: before distilling a develop run, check whether the run's seed is already closed on the base branch (duplicate-run detection), so a duplicate run cannot pass review as healthy.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-09T12:24:30.496Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-652d","title":"Engine: batch checkpoint pushes at terminal/soft-exit boundaries instead of every stage boundary","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T11:40:44.623Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T11:52:33.005Z","description":"Engine checkpoint pipeline: keep per-stage commits but push only at terminal or soft-exit boundaries. Grounded in run 01M22YZBNJ0Y06H8C8C0G3VN3W: active stage time 95.4 s vs 141.6 s wall; each of 5 stage boundaries cost ~5 s (snapshot 2.1 s + commit + push; implementer done 11:32:44.4 -> tester start 11:32:49.1) and the terminal segment (final push + PR creation) took 17 s. Tester/evidence/closeout are command nodes that get full commit+push treatment. Orthogonal to open seeds fabro-c2ca (skip snapshots on non-agent stages) and fabro-cf03 (snapshot async/branch-point-only) — neither covers push cadence. Expected effect: ~10-20 s (~10%) off every develop run's wall time, independent of seed size.\nBasis: run 01M22YZBNJ0Y06H8C8C0G3VN3W, workflow version 14ab451ff2f9375f4927ce7d994c63bc96f48f3c617f3baff15119472f3af3e4, commit 2168350e49d7e7c63a09dcd996ae773f7cc8a46f","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
